{
  "_comment": [
    "Expectations for `junit-metrics.ts` over the four-leg baseline.",
    "`requiredTests` are the nine timeout-shaped tests the predecessor fix's",
    "acceptance criterion 4 measures plus two Phase 3 additions: their absence",
    "from a leg is a gate failure, so a run that silently stopped executing one",
    "cannot read as a speed-up. Every one of them lives in a `#![cfg(unix)]`",
    "binary (`wrap_watchdog_timeout`, `sequence_schema`, `wrap_opencode`,",
    "`compose_schema_cli`, `composition_outputs`), so `windows-latest` cannot",
    "run them: `platformExclusions` declares that, and the gate reports the",
    "absence apart from violations while failing if one ever *does* run there.",
    "`enforceTimeoutFloors` stays false for the baseline because those floors were",
    "ratified under the pre-fix first-event grace; Phase 3 re-derives them under",
    "the 2026-08-31 spawn-fallback silence clock and Phase 9 turns enforcement on",
    "for the candidate sets (`../candidate/expectations.json`)."
  ],
  "environments": ["ubuntu-latest", "macos-latest", "windows-latest", "wsl2-ubuntu"],
  "cells": [
    { "tier": "L1", "package": "claudine-cli" }
  ],
  "requiredTests": [
    "watchdog_subagent_hang_terminates_and_names_stuck_ids",
    "watchdog_stream_idle_timeout_after_tool_call_hang",
    "watchdog_wall_clock_timeout_terminates_active_stream",
    "watchdog_opencode_post_fanout_silence_does_not_kill_prematurely",
    "compose_non_harness_respects_cli_timeout",
    "inline_compose_non_harness_respects_cli_step_timeout",
    "sequence_per_step_step_timeout_override",
    "opencode_stderr_rate_limit_before_stdout_forces_early_termination",
    "opencode_stderr_stream_error_cap_1_17_8_forces_early_termination",
    "inline_compose_wrong_type_prompt_takes_precedence_over_schema_scrub",
    "a_loop_accumulates_outputs_and_retains_mutations_across_iterations"
  ],
  "pendingEnvironments": [],
  "platformExclusions": {
    "windows-latest": [
      "watchdog_subagent_hang_terminates_and_names_stuck_ids",
